		"tokens",
		"base",
		"layout",
		"patterns",
		"components",
		"vendor",
		"utilities"
	],
	"$sheets": "Every stylesheet, in <link> order, which is layer order — a sheet's directory is its layer, and the groups appear in the order above. The one exception is base/fonts.css, linked ahead of the theme paint for the fetch and holding nothing but @font-face, which the cascade never arbitrates. Each entry carries the layer it declares and the selector roots it owns. A root is the bare name a selector leads with, as scripts/lint-css-arch computes it: the leading element, class or id with its punctuation dropped, skipping :root/html/body when the selector descends past them. A selector that names two sheets' roots — the scope it leads with, and a name on the subject compound it ends with — may be filed under either. A `*` in a pattern is a glob. An entry starting `--` claims custom-property and @keyframes names only, never a root (README ▸ Naming). One group is one sheet — a group's rules are never spread across two of them.",
